---
# Clang-Tidy configuration for gleditor
# Kept in harmony with .clangd via tools/check-config-harmony.sh
#
# Checks disabled below beyond clang-tidy's stock defaults, grouped by why (a
# YAML block-scalar value can't carry per-line comments, so the reasoning
# lives here instead of next to each `-check` entry):
#
# Required by C APIs and the low-level memory management this project does
# on purpose -- mmap'd arenas/spools with pointer-offset access, binary wire
# formats needing reinterpret_cast, POSIX file I/O taking C varargs, and a
# handful of C APIs (LMDB) that take a non-const pointer to logically-const
# data:
#   pro-type-const-cast, pro-type-reinterpret-cast, pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
#   pro-bounds-constant-array-index, pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay, pro-type-vararg
#
# Fire on idiomatic C/C++ this codebase uses throughout; not real ambiguity:
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion (if (ptr), std::isdigit() returning
#   int used as bool), readability-math-missing-parentheses (flags ordinary,
#   universally-understood `*` vs `+` precedence)
#
# Conflict with an established, deliberate pattern in this codebase rather
# than catching a defect:
#   cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes (protected
#   members are the controlled-inheritance-access pattern used throughout,
#   e.g. Drawable::model, Doc's shaping state), avoid-const-or-ref-data-members
#   (non-owning back-references, e.g. a11y::Tree&), avoid-non-const-global-variables
#   (module-local mutexes and memoization caches, which are non-const by
#   nature), readability-braces-around-statements (this codebase's own
#   single-line guard-clause style, `if (x) return;`)
#
# Legitimate and possibly worth doing, but out of scope for a mechanical
# pass: each needs deliberate per-site engineering judgment (is this class's
# copy semantics actually safe to default, would this enum's implicit
# conversions matter at a specific call site) rather than a bulk edit, and
# getting one wrong risks a real bug (a resource-holding class becoming
# silently copyable, or losing an implicit conversion callers relied on).
# Disabled here rather than fixed case-by-case; worth a dedicated pass later:
#   cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions, cppcoreguidelines-use-enum-class,
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays, cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays (std::array is a
#   safe drop-in for most of these, but 298 sites is a dedicated pass, not this one)
#
# A refactoring-backlog signal (this function is complex, consider splitting
# it), not a discrete defect with a fix -- tracked as future work rather than
# something a warnings pass resolves:
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#
# Portable on every compiler this project targets (clang, gcc); the
# alternative (traditional #ifndef include guards) is pure churn for no
# actual portability gain here:
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once
#
# A micro-optimization with no safe auto-fix and low value outside
# size-critical structs, which already specify explicit underlying types on
# purpose (e.g. CompactOpNode's bitfields, migration step 8's ruling in
# design/store-slice-convergence.md) rather than relying on the compiler to
# shrink an enum:
#   performance-enum-size
#
# Legitimate checks whose *auto-fix* is unsafe for patterns this codebase
# relies on -- confirmed by actually running run-clang-tidy -fix and finding
# broken code, not by inspection alone. Left enabled for manual review
# (dropped from any future -fix run, kept as an editor/CI diagnostic):
#   modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison: rewrites `x == static_cast<Unsigned>(-1)`
#   (this codebase's `noCell`/"unlimited" sentinel idiom, e.g.
#   zigzag::walkRank's maxSteps default, VortexCore::link's allocation-form
#   check) into `std::cmp_equal(x, -1)`, which can never be true for an
#   unsigned x -- silently inverting the check. Caused three real test
#   failures (VortexHostTest, VortexCoreTest) before being caught.
#   modernize-use-ranges: `std::search`/similar algorithms return an
#   iterator; `std::ranges::search` returns a subrange, breaking any
#   `it == container.end()` comparison at the call site the fix doesn't
#   update. Also hit std::sortable/concept requirements classic std::sort
#   didn't enforce, failing to compile for a type this codebase sorts
#   deliberately with a bare operator<.
#   readability-convert-member-functions-to-static: reorders an existing
#   [[nodiscard]] to *after* the new `static`, which changes what the
#   attribute grammatically attaches to and fails to compile.
#   readability-non-const-parameter: added `const` to pointer parameters of
#   a libvlc callback, changing its signature away from what
#   libvlc_video_set_format_callbacks requires and failing to compile.
#   bugprone-macro-parentheses: cannot tell a macro parameter used as a type
#   name (GLEDITOR_NON_COPYABLE(Type) in sdl_wrap.hpp) from one used as a
#   value, and wraps the type in parentheses, breaking every expansion.
#   cppcoreguidelines-prefer-member-initializer: moves a member's assignment
#   into the constructor initializer list without checking whether the moved
#   expression depends on another member that is only computed later in the
#   constructor *body* -- initializer-list order follows declaration order,
#   not source order, so the moved expression can silently read a
#   not-yet-initialized value. Two real bugs: VPLEngine and
#   MultiStoreCoordinator's owned-pointer-plus-raw-alias pattern (core_ set
#   from ownedCore_.get() before ownedCore_ was assigned in the body, leaving
#   core_ permanently null -- a real segfault caught by
#   VQLMultiStoreTest.CoordinatorGenesis), and Page::Page's originX/originY
#   moved ahead of the pageWidth/pageHeight the body computes from
#   pageBoxFor() -- silently wrong page origins, uncaught by any test.
Checks: >
  -*,
  modernize-*,
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  portability-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -modernize-use-std-print,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-const-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions,
  -cppcoreguidelines-use-enum-class,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -performance-enum-size
HeaderFilterRegex: '^(include|src|apps)/'
WarningsAsErrors: ''
...
